Received a very simple and clean script from Mark, using the timezone =
looking forward without hardcoding the timezone.  Here it is:

________________________________________
>From Mark Deiss

D=3D$(TZ=3D`date +%Z`-24 date +%d)=20
if [ "$D" =3D "01" -o "${D}" =3D "1" ]; then=20
        echo today is the last day of the month=20
        echo execute something=20
fi=20

date +%Z pull out the current time zone on the server; you could hard =
code it to whatever is the fixed time zone value (i.e. TZ=3DEST-24 ).

date +%Z-24 advances the time zone one day - getting you the next day=20
date +%d displays the next day - some implementations may pad with a =
leading zero so the if statement that follows should handle either =
representation of the first of the next month.
______________________________________

Thanks Mark!

Best Regards,	Blake
